^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-08-24 10:00] observe — VS Code and Neovim already expose shared LSP probes; IntelliJ native LSP provides standard rename but not the custom-request lane.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:01] decide — preserve native LSP rename for caret edits and reserve the CLI refactor command for explicit read-only corpus plans.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:02] taste — command names should transfer between terminal and editor while each editor retains native presentation and cancellation behavior.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:03] decide — use tool-root selection for npm prefix and consumer-root selection for process cwd so mounted infrastructure never takes consumer authority.
 >>[2026-08-24 14:40] implement — added pure Kotlin, TypeScript, and Lua invocation models for form, stack, cache, and plan-only corpus refactoring.
 >>[2026-08-24 14:55] decide — IntelliJ results open as read-only typed preview files; this preserves reusable JSON/Spw output without introducing a persistent tool window before repeated-use evidence exists.
 >>[2026-08-24 14:56] implement — added explicit background IntelliJ actions for saved-file form, stack, cache, native LSP rename, and plan-only corpus refactoring.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:15] revise — normalized receipts name their actual layer rather than flattening CLI, LSP session reflection, and the VS Code TTL probe cache into one cache claim.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:16] implement — extracted VS Code instruments from the oversized command registry and added concise Neovim Form → Stack → Cache → Rename → RefactorPlan commands.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:42] taste — shared questions should make cross-editor comparison possible without flattening host contour: VS Code guides and compares, IntelliJ outlines and refactors natively, Neovim composes terse buffers and commands.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:43] revise — registered editor-instruments as the canon contract for question parity, provenance receipts, creative host contours, and plan-only corpus effects.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:45] verify — TypeScript build, 226 LSP tests, 8 VS Code tests and bundle, Neovim headless smoke, Writerside references, plan health, and Spw corpus lint pass; IntelliJ build and verifier mark WebStorm 2026.2.0.1 and 2026.2.1 compatible with nine bounded native-LSP deprecations retained for the 242–262 range.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:46] publish — documented the shared sequence and distinct host contours, registered the canon contract and evaluation target, and refreshed the adjacent editor, performance, refactor, and plan-ecology surfaces.
 >>[2026-08-24 18:00] revise — host completeness is not a goal. Form, stack, and cache remain because they disclose structure, profile, and memo plane; a missing receipt is a kernel or runtime question.
 >>[2026-08-24 18:20] revise — depth and parity are the design tension. Peer hosts should reach the same receipts; native chrome may differ. Do not treat mimicry as parity or one host as the real product.
}

